From 4b5965e6196810a3813a6d2092ac1bf1c9ebda50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:28:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] EAP-PEAP server: Fix SoH vendor-specific TLV length check to
 require 8 bytes

eap_peap_process_phase2_soh() checks that a vendor-specific
Statement-of-Health TLV is at least 4 bytes long before reading the
4-byte vendor_id at that offset:

    if (tlv_len < 4) { ... reject ... }
    vendor_id = WPA_GET_BE32(pos);

but the following lines unconditionally read a second, inner 4-byte TLV
header starting 4 bytes further in:

    vpos = pos + 4;
    mandatory = !!(vpos[0] & 0x80);
    tlv_type = (vpos[0] & 0x3f) << 8 | vpos[1];
    vtlv_len = (vpos[2] << 8) | vpos[3];

so the minimum required length is 8 bytes, not 4. With tlv_len == 4 and
this TLV positioned at the end of the received SoH buffer, the vpos[]
reads run past the end of the buffer -- a heap out-of-bounds read of
attacker-controlled (EAP peer supplied) data.

Require tlv_len >= 8 before reading the inner TLV header.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Arrendondo <brandon.arrendondo@bissell.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4b5965e6196810a3813a6d2092ac1bf1c9ebda50)
---
 src/eap_server/eap_server_peap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/eap_server/eap_server_peap.c b/src/eap_server/eap_server_peap.c
index 998d0e8ae..07f4c9151 100644
--- a/src/eap_server/eap_server_peap.c
+++ b/src/eap_server/eap_server_peap.c
@@ -861,7 +861,7 @@ static void eap_peap_process_phase2_soh(struct eap_sm *sm,
 		}
 		switch (tlv_type) {
 		case EAP_TLV_VENDOR_SPECIFIC_TLV:
-			if (tlv_len < 4) {
+			if (tlv_len < 8) {
 				wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "EAP-PEAP: Too short "
 					   "vendor specific TLV (len=%d)",
 					   (int) tlv_len);
